  "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{7x-8}+5 & <1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7x-8} & <-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the square root is less than a negative number $(-4),$ so no number that we can substitute into the square root will satisfy the inequality.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality.",
